{
  "cand-scout#1": "# iamwavecut/ninfer-all — consolidated NInfer line (RTX 3090 candidate scout)\n\n## 1. Repo / release / commit\n- URL: https://github.com/iamwavecut/ninfer-all (fork-line consolidating Neroued/ninfer → Don-Chad/ninfer-3090 → ashalliants/ninfer-3090 + TertiumOrganum1, UDPSendToFailed/ninfer-4090, Wallawalla47, IMGillusion, MirkoCovizzi, gzenz, tmark00; base = ashalliants v0.12.0)\n- NO GitHub Releases and NO tags (\"There aren't any releases here\" on /releases page; /tags API returned HTTP 403). Distribution = `ghcr.io/iamwavecut/ninfer-all:latest` container (tags: `latest`, `sha-<commit>`, `VERSION`; 1.6 GB compressed, CUDA 13.4/Ubuntu 26.04, dual builds sm_86 + sm_120a, auto-selects per GPU) or build from source.\n- HEAD @ 2026-10-08: `64492cb14d246fa04a5241c42e771dcfdff40753` (2026-10-07, \"feat(qwen4_exp): MTP speculative decoding and the n-gram table's residencies\").\n- Reference-measurement builds: card cites `master` at `2172a598` (Sept 2026); quality tables at engine `897f89a3`; Oct re-check built `796f98500` sm_120a. Version string pattern `v0.12.0-41-g<sha>`. Pin recommendation: `64492cb` (master) or the sha-tagged image.\n\n## 2. Build / serve invocations (exact)\nNative sm_86 build (docs/rtx-3090-linux.md; CUDA 12.8+ for `86`, configure refuses 12.8/12.9 only for `120a`):\n```bash\nexport CC=/usr/bin/gcc-13 CXX=/usr/bin/g++-13 CUDACXX=/usr/local/cuda/bin/nvcc CUDAHOSTCXX=/usr/bin/g++-13\ncmake -S . -B build-sm86 -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \\\n  -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=\"$CC\" -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=\"$CXX\" -DCMAKE_CUDA_COMPILER=\"$CUDACXX\" \\\n  -DCMAKE_CUDA_HOST_COMPILER=\"$CUDAHOSTCXX\" -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=86 \\\n  -DNINFER_BUILD_APPS=ON -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF -DNINFER_BUILD_BENCHMARKS=OFF\ncmake --build build-sm86 --parallel 2\n# → build-sm86/apps/{ninfer,ninfer-serve,ninfer-calibrate,ninfer-perplexity}\n```\nOpt-in CMake: `NINFER_SFU_SIGMOID_SILU`, `NINFER_SFU_SOFTPLUS`, `NINFER_BF16_RESIDUAL_ADD`, `NINFER_MULTICALL=ON` (one ~0.5 GB/arch kernel image + symlinks; container uses this), `NINFER_NVCC_SPLIT_COMPILE=N`, `NINFER_WEBUI_DIR`. Runtime env: `NINFER_CUDA_SYNC=spin|blocking|yield|auto`, `NINFER_T2_A8_TILE=off`, `NINFER_PREFILL_ALIGN=0`, `NINFER_DEVICE_PROFILES`.\n\nServe — Qwen3.8-27B official artifact (launcher `tuned` profile, dflash2 fast path, from scripts/run.sh):\n```bash\nninfer-serve models/qwen3_8_27b.ninfer \\\n  --max-concurrency 1 --max-context 262144 --kv-capacity 262144 --kv-dtype rk4v4 \\\n  --spec dflash2 --draft-tokens 7 --lm-head-draft \\\n  --embedding-q4 --gdn-state-fp16 --prefill-cublas --prefill-chunk 4096 \\\n  --vision --vision-residency overlay --max-pending-requests 16 --pending-timeout-ms 600000 \\\n  --max-private-continuations 8 --max-shared-prefixes 8 --host-state-slots 32 --host-kv-mib 8192 --auto-prefix-grid\n```\nAlternative spec (`NINFER_SPEC=mtp`): `--spec mtp --draft-tokens 3 --lm-head-draft --lm-head-q6 ... --prefill-chunk 2048`, C=2; `none` = no spec, C=2. Launcher auto-steps context down /8 (229376→65536) on OOM unless `NINFER_FALLBACK=off`. Reference protocol itself uses minimal flags (no launcher extras): `ninfer-serve <artifact> --max-context W --kv-capacity W --max-concurrency 1 --kv-dtype <KV> --gdn-state-fp16 [--spec dflash2 --draft-tokens 5 | --spec mtp --draft-tokens 3] [--lm-head-draft]`, `--rope-yarn` past 262,144.\n\nServe — Bonsai 2 27B (README recipe): `--max-context 262144 --kv-capacity 262144 --kv-dtype rk8v4 --gdn-state-fp16 --spec dflash2 --draft-tokens 5` (MTP variant: `--spec mtp --draft-tokens 3 --lm-head-draft`; max context on 3090: 958,464 with `--kv-dtype rk4v4 --rope-yarn`).\nServe — GSQ-RCO IQ3_S: `--model-id qwen3.8-27b --kv-dtype rk8v4 --gdn-state-fp16 --spec mtp --draft-tokens 3` at 176,128 (3090).\n\nConcurrency flags: `--max-concurrency N`, shared pool `--kv-capacity`, `--device-state-slots`, `--host-state-slots`/`--host-kv-mib` (or single `--host-cache-mib`), `--adaptive-mtp` (verifies 3..K), `--mtp-attention-window N`. Router mode: `--models-dir`/`--models-preset` + `--models-max` + `--model-suspend` (two 27B models swap on one 24 GB card in 1.8 s vs 11.6 s cold load; suspend frees 7.9 GiB→0.3 GiB in 0.33 s, resumes 1.1 s).\nSpec-decode: `--spec mtp|dflash|dflash2 --draft-tokens 1..15`, `--lm-head-draft` (proposal head). DFlash2 best at 5–7 drafts short answers, 3–7 after long docs; MTP best at 3–5 (11–15 only for near-copy coding tasks, up to 1.85×). Context: `--max-context N` (per-request ceiling), `--kv-capacity N|auto` (pool; `auto` sizes from free VRAM, `--kv-headroom-mib` default 1024). Quant/artifact selection = choose HF artifact file; runtime quant knobs: `--kv-dtype bf16|int8|fp8|rk8v4|rk4v4|rk4v4-e8|rk2v4-e8|nvfp4|k8v4`, `--embedding-q4`, `--lm-head-q4/q6`, `--gdn-state-fp16`, `--prefill-cublas`.\n\n## 3. Model artifacts (exact files, sizes, fit-on-24 GB)\n| model | artifact (single .ninfer file) | size | source |\n|---|---|---:|---|\n| Ternary Bonsai 2 27B | `Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-ninfer-v3.ninfer` | 9,520,051,456 B = 8.87 GiB (sha256 `cdc4810b…3c14a`) | HF `WaveCut/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-NInfer-v3` |\n| Qwen3.8-27B official (groupwise Q4/Q5 + MTP + DFlash2 in one file) | `qwen3_8_27b.ninfer` | 20,437,521,664 B = 19.0 GiB (sha256 `81f924d4…75da`, pin revision `1cbd84e7221e51186bd7f093a149912d2489625b`) | HF `neroued/Qwen3.8-27B-NInfer` |\n| Qwen3.8-27B GSQ-RCO IQ3_S (3.5-bit, +MTP+DFlash2+Vision+proposal head) | `Qwen3.8-27B-GSQ-RCO-IQ3_S-ninfer-v3.ninfer` | 15,017,456,896 B = 13.99 GiB | HF `WaveCut/Qwen3.8-27B-GSQ-RCO-IQ3_S-NInfer-v3` |\n\nDownload: `hf download <repo> <file> --local-dir models`, or `docker run … ghcr.io/iamwavecut/ninfer-all download qwen38-27b` (only official Qwen3.8/Qwen3.6 pinned in `scripts/download-model.sh`; aria2c 16-range). Offline conversion from GGUF: `python3 -m tools.convert --recipe bonsai2_27b_ternary|qwen3_8_27b_gguf --source ternary=…/gguf=… --components text,vision,mtp,dflash2 --proposal --out …`.\n\n262K-context fit on 24 GB (GPU-resident, engine pre-reserves ALL VRAM at startup — no CPU offload path exists for dense-model weights/KV; host tiers only apply to Flash-Next experts and checkpoint/KV spillover):\n- **Bonsai 2 27B: YES, comfortably.** Idle VRAM @262,144 window, text-only: rk4v4 12.2 GiB / rk8v4 14.2 GiB; +MTP3 12.9/15.0; +DFlash2-5 13.7/15.7. Largest 3090 windows: rk4v4 970,752 (no spec) / 884,736 (MTP3) / 839,680 (DFlash2-5); rk4v4-e8 970,752 (no spec); rk8v4 663,552/606,208/585,728. rk4v4-e8 = 280 B/token/head (saves 2.0 GiB vs rk8v4 at 262K, ppl 5.631→5.650); rk2v4-e8 = 216 B/token/head (only format fitting 1,048,576 beside Bonsai on 24 GB; ppl 5.820, DFlash2 acc 54.4→51.8%, decode −4%).\n- **Qwen3.8-27B official: PARTIAL.** rk4v4 DFlash2-5 = 23.6 GiB @258,048 tokens fits a headless 24 GB (run.sh extrapolation; ~1.45 GB more needed beside a desktop → step-down). rk4v4 MTP3 22.0 GiB @258,048; rk4v4 none 21.3 GiB @258,048; rk4v4-e8 none 21.4 GiB @262,144 (only no-spec fits full window); rk8v4 DFlash2 25.8 GiB > 24 GB → window cut to 176,128. Largest 3090 windows: rk4v4 417,792/364,544/258,048; rk8v4 286,720/249,856/176,128; rk4v4-e8 417,792.\n- **Qwen3.8 IQ3_S: YES.** 10.95 GiB weights (13.99 GiB file); 59.9 vs 40.3 tok/s of official on 3090; same KV windows as above (doc quotes 176,128 rk8v4 MTP3 recipe).\n- `ninfer-all` README: upstream artifacts also load (official NInfer artifacts compatible).\n\n## 4. Native OpenAI-compatible server: YES\n`ninfer-serve` (port 8080 default; container binds 0.0.0.0:8080): OpenAI Chat Completions `POST /v1/chat/completions` (stream + non-stream), OpenAI Completions `POST /v1/completions`, **Anthropic Messages** (`/v1/messages`), llama.cpp-style raw `POST /completion`, Responses API, `GET /v1/models`, `GET /models`+`/models/load|unload|sleep|sse` (router), `POST /v1/models/{id}/suspend|/resume`, `/tokenize`, `/detokenize`, `/apply-template`, `POST /v1/rerank`, `/slots`, `/props`, `/v1/load`, `/metrics`, `/stats` (`--stats-port`), structured output (`response_format json_schema` via xgrammar), logprobs. This is an OpenAI+Anthropic+llama.cpp-compatible surface — NOT a generate-style-only endpoint.\n\n## 5. Published benchmark protocol (in-repo)\n- `docs/performance/reference-2026-09.md` — full Sept 2026 campaign: Bonsai 2 + Qwen3.8-27B on RTX 3090/4090/5090/PRO 6000; per-KV-code decode-vs-depth tables (1K→261K), TTFT, draft acceptance, NIAH needle checks, largest-context bisection (4,096-step), draft-length sweeps 1–15, 8-request concurrency table. Hardware: rented hosts, RTX 3090 390 W (Bonsai rows) / 370 W (Qwen rows), server pinned to GPU NUMA node.\n- `tools/bench/refbench.py` (341 lines, the reference client): suites `idle|warmup|depth|accept|conc|niah` against `/v1/chat/completions`; greedy, non-streaming, thinking off, fresh nonce per request (no prefix reuse); NVML memory sampling every 0.2 s with per-row peak; TTFT from server `timings.prompt_ms`; decode tok/s = (completion_tokens−1)/`predicted_ms`; acceptance = `draft_n_accepted/draft_n`; `conc` = aggregate tok/s over wall time with `--conc-depth` documents; `niah` = 3 codes at 33/66/90%. Rows → JSONL, resumable via key dedup. Usage: `python3 tools/bench/refbench.py --base-url http://127.0.0.1:8080 --model <id> --depths 1024 8192 32768 … --conc 1 2 4 8 …` (argparse tail not fetched; flags seen in code: `--depths`, `--reps`, `--gen`, `--depth-question short|long`, `--accept-gen`, `--conc`, `--conc-depth`, `--niah`, `--keep-text`, `--out`).\n- Also `ninfer-perplexity --quick|--disjoint` (WikiText-2 protocol), `eval/README.md` capability evals (EvalScope), `tools/monitor` dashboard/watchdog.\n\n## 6. Their published RTX 3090 numbers (ground truth to replicate)\nBonsai 2 27B @262,144 (rk8v4 unless noted): short chat 94.1 (none) / 172.2 (MTP3) / 201.4 (DFlash2-5) / 202.0 (DFlash2-7) tok/s; decode after 261K 50.0 (none) / 89.7 (DFlash2-5) tok/s; TTFT 32K 13.1 s / 131K 76.2 s / 261K 214.5 s; 8×MTP3 total 551 tok/s (4 at once: 413.7). Qwen3.8-27B: short chat 48.2 (none) / 117.1 (DFlash2-5) tok/s; TTFT 32K 23.1 s; TTFT 261K n/a (window 258,048: 297.5 s at depth); 8×MTP3 328.9 tok/s. Idle VRAM as in §3. Device-profile gains on 3090: rk4v4 verify attention ≤3.20×, fast prompt kernel 1.41×, FP16 PV 1.17×.\n\n## 7. Risk flags\n- **OOM at 24 GB**: engine pre-reserves whole KV pool + graphs at startup (VRAM never grows under load → startup failure instead of mid-run OOM). Documented over-budget configs: Qwen3.8 rk8v4 DFlash2-5 25.8 GiB and rk8v4 MTP3 24.4 GiB at full window — must step window down (176,128 / 249,856). Launcher has auto step-down; `NINFER_FALLBACK=off` to disable. rk8v4 8-lane ×16,384 KV does not fit for Qwen3.8 (falls to 4 lanes); 3090 \"Qwen3.8 DFlash2 at 8\" cell is a dash. `--kv-capacity auto` + `--kv-headroom-mib` sizes safely.\n- **Patched CUDA**: NONE required. sm_86 is the DEFAULT `CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES`; CUDA 12.8+; `120a` (not needed on 3090) requires CUDA ≥13.1 because 12.8/12.9 miscompile sm_120a. Whole-program CUDA build (no RDC). Published image checked on a real RTX 3090 (driver 580.159.03, CUDA-13-branch driver ≥580 required for container).\n- **sm_86 support**: first-class — built-in device route profile `nvidia-geforce-rtx-3090-sm86` (82 SMs) compiled into the binary; `ninfer-calibrate` for refresh. FP8/NVFP4 tensor-core features are Blackwell-only and refused on sm_86 (relevant: NVFP4 artifacts refuse to load on sm_86; `sm_8x` builds refuse NVFP4 expert banks). Old-engine artifact-compat caveats exist (Bonsai v3 artifact needs ≥ `1e9e01e1`/`2172a598`-era master; older builds fail `q4 linear: unsupported shape`).\n- **Ternary artifact lock-in**: `Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-ninfer-v3.ninfer` (t2_g128_fp16 + hadamard_signs) is explicitly refused by stock Neroued/ninfer — only this consolidated line reads it.\n- CPU offload: dense-model weights/KV are GPU-resident by design; the only host-RAM consumers are optional pinned context-cache/state pools (`--host-state-slots` 74.5 MiB/slot on 27B, `--host-kv-mib` 8192 default in tuned ≈ 74.5 MiB×32 + 8 GiB ≈ 10.4 GB pinned) — tune `--host-state-slots`/`--host-cache-mib` down to minimize host RAM. No weights/KV spill path exists."
