  "cand-scout#2": "# signalnine/q27 (Quasar) — scout report (verified 2026-10-08)\n\n## 1. Repo / release / commit\n- Repo: https://github.com/signalnine/q27 — CUDA C++ (no deps beyond CUDA runtime + httplib/json vendored), MIT. Single tri-arch binary: CLI `q27` + server `q27-server`.\n- Latest release: **v0.14.4** (2026-10-08 03:27 UTC), tag commit **`1eb10b0`** (full: 1eb10b01948dba2212639b05dc972a7aca50e867). Master HEAD = `e86672702f478702fb989f9c3bad07e22ff527fe` (1 commit past tag at fetch time).\n- Release assets: `q27-v0.14.4-linux-x86_64.tar.gz` + `SHA256SUMS-0.14.4` containing `q27`, `q27-server`, `q27-server-w8`, `q27-server-w16` (sm_86+sm_89+sm_120/120a) and `q27-server-12g` (sm_86 only, 8–12 GB Bonsai build), built with CUDA 13.2, CUDA runtime statically linked, needs driver **r580+**, glibc 2.38+. Older hosts: build from source against CUDA 12.8 (`deploy/runpod-serverless/Dockerfile.source`, driver r570+).\n\n## 2. Build / serve invocations (exact)\nBuild (requires CUDA toolkit 12.8+ at /usr/local/cuda — 12.8 is a hard floor because the build links an sm_120a object unconditionally; gcc; `make` builds one tri-arch binary sm_86+sm_89+sm_120, arch dispatch at runtime):\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/signalnine/q27 && cd q27\nmake                        # default width-12 server\nmake build/q27-server-w8    # 24GB (3090-class): -DQ27_W_MAX=8 — USE THIS on 24GB; the default w12 build OOMs at graph setup\nmake build/q27-server-12g   # 8-12GB Bonsai slim packs (sm_86-only, W_MAX=8, 256-row prefill chunks)\n```\nServe (smoke test first):\n```bash\n./build/q27 ../models/qwen36-27b-mtp/qwen36-27b-mtp.q27 --tokens \"760,6511,314,9338,369\" -n 128 --ctx 2048 --spec\n./build/q27-server ../models/qwen36-27b-mtp/qwen36-27b-mtp.q27 ../models/qwen36-27b-mtp/qwen36-27b-mtp.tok --port 8080\n```\n- **max-context**: `--ctx` auto-sizes to measured free VRAM (recalibrated 2026-07-17); `--slots N` with auto-ctx gives elastic shared KV pool (any slot may hold the whole pool; banker's-algorithm growth; `Q27_KV_INCREMENTAL=0` restores up-front reservation). KV format env `Q27_KV=fp8|fp16|turbo3|turbo5k` (server default: fp8 on sm_89+, **turbo5k on Ampere/sm_86**; `Q27_KV=turbo3` = 14.1 KB/token; turbo3@262144 on 3090 measured, needle 6/6 at ~233K prompt).\n- **concurrency**: `--slots N` (conductor fused rounds; `Q27_BATCH=1` default, continuous batching default since 2026-07-16; `Q27_BATCH=0` for single-slot/DFlash2). Sub-24GiB cards: `Q27_MAXD=4 Q27_SAMPLED=0` (A10 22.6 GiB boots full 262,144; issue #1). Single-slot Bonsai: `Q27_BATCH=0` (conductor k=1 fused round costs 15–20%). Related env: `Q27_PMIN` (adaptive depth 4..7, bitwise-neutral), `Q27_DFLASH2_K` (K=7 default), `Q27_PRINT_WSUM=1` + `Q27_EXPECT_WSUM` (load-digest corruption gate), `Q27_FIXED_STACK_GB`, `Q27_WAIT_LOG_MS`, `Q27_REQ_LOG`, `Q27_API_KEY`.\n- **spec-decode modes**: (a) trained-in **MTP ladder** (default; fused shared-KV MMA verify, suffix drafter width 12); (b) **DFlash2 block drafter** — env `Q27_DFLASH2=<pack>.d2w Q27_BATCH=0 Q27_DFLASH2_RESERVE_GB=3` (single-slot only; K=7 via `Q27_DFLASH2_K`); (c) Bonsai multi-slot: T2+MTP pack with `Q27_BATCH=1` and no DFlash2. Pack for Bonsai2 mode in `tools/launch_q27_38.sh` (modes: `d2|d2-pfx|ladder|bonsai2`; extra `-E K=V` pass-through).\n- **quant/artifact selection**: artifact filename IS the tier (`.q27` packs; engine auto-detects Bonsai container, activation rotation, XML tool dialect `qwen38` from name; `repack.py --name` for fine-tunes whose names lack `qwen38`). Full production recipe script: `tools/launch_q27_38.sh`.\n\n## 3. Model artifacts (exact names, sizes, sources) — 24GB fit without CPU offload\nq27 has NO CPU-offload path at all — weights/KV/state are GPU-resident by design; host RAM is only pinned staging + optional prefix-cache tiers (RAM tier off by default).\n\nQwen3.8-27B-MTP tiers — https://huggingface.co/signalnine/Qwen3.8-27B-MTP-q27 (v2 recipes; lastModified 2026-09-09):\n| file | size |\n|---|---|\n| `qwen38-27b-mtp-q4s.q27` | 15.70 GB (15,704,702,464 B) |\n| `qwen38-27b-mtp.q27` (default v2) | 17.00 GB (16,995,966,464 B) |\n| `qwen38-27b-mtp-q6.q27` | 19.76 GB |\n| `qwen38-27b-mtp-q6k.q27` | 22.52 GB |\n| `qwen38-27b-mtp.tok` | 7.2 MB |\n| `qwen38-dflash2-q8-serve.d2w` (DFlash2 drafter pack) | 2.08 GB |\n| `qwen38-dflash2-q4-serve.d2w` | 1.21 GB |\nNote: item brief's \"q5f\" tier exists only for **Qwen3.6-27B-MTP** (`signalnine/Qwen3.6-27B-MTP-q27`: default 5.25 bpw, q4s 4.55, q5f 5.30, q6/q6f/q6k 32GB, q8 48GB). For **Qwen3.8 v2** the 24GB tiers are q4s/default/q6. Fits 24GB: q4s and default yes (262K needs turbo3/turbo5k KV; q6 19.76 GB leaves ~2GB → tight; q6k does not fit with stack).\nAgentic fine-tune: `signalnine/Qwen3.8-27B-pi-q27` (bytkim/Qwen3.8-27B-pi port, 2026-10-05).\n\nTernary Bonsai 2 27B — https://huggingface.co/signalnine/Bonsai-2-27B-q27 (lastModified 2026-09-22; exact re-encode of `prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-gguf` `Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-PTQ1_0.gguf`; native T2_G128/T3_G128 containers, Hadamard-rotated, Q8 embed/head):\n| file | size | notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `bonsai2-27b-t2.q27` | 9.44 GB (9,440,154,880 B) | single-slot serving, DFlash2-only drafter; wsum `9161ec16da4b66a1` |\n| `bonsai2-27b-t2-mtp.q27` | 9.87 GB (9,871,569,152 B) | + ProCreations MTP head as blk.64; **multi-slot** (`--slots 8 --ctx 16384`, `Q27_BATCH=1`); needs v0.13.0+; wsum `0f85b21f8721e39c` |\n| `bonsai2-27b-t3-slim.q27` | 6.06 GB | T3_G128 body (5 trits/byte, 1.6 bpw), bitwise the T2 pack; needs v0.14.0+; 8GB cards |\n| `bonsai2-27b-t3-mtp-slim.q27` | 6.49 GB | T3 + MTP head |\n| `qwen38-27b-mtp.tok` | 7.2 MB | tokenizer |\nDownload: `hf download signalnine/Bonsai-2-27B-q27 --local-dir models/bonsai2` + `md5sum -c CHECKSUMS.md5`. 24GB fit: trivially — 9.44 GB weights + ~2.3 GB engine stack leaves ~12 GB KV → full 262,144 native window on turbo3/turbo5k without offload (on 32GB they report 23 GB KV free / auto ctx 262K). Rebuild from source GGUF: `python3 tools/repack.py Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-PTQ1_0.gguf out.q27 [--bonsai2-container t3 --slim] [--mtp-safetensors model_mtp.safetensors]` (~3 min, numpy only; ProCreations drafter packs via `tools/dflash2_pack.py <dir> bonsai2-dflash2-q8-serve.d2w --q8`).\nServing (Bonsai 2, single-slot DFlash2, Qwen3.8-drafter variant):\n```bash\nQ27_KV=fp8 Q27_BATCH=0 Q27_DFLASH2=models/qwen38/qwen38-dflash2-q8-serve.d2w Q27_DFLASH2_RESERVE_GB=3 \\\n  ./build/q27-server models/bonsai2/bonsai2-27b-t2.q27 models/bonsai2/qwen38-27b-mtp.tok \\\n  --think --temp 1.0 --top-p 0.95 --top-k 20 --min-p 0.05 --think-budget 0\n```\n(Bonsai-trained drafter: point `Q27_DFLASH2` at `bonsai2-dflash2-q8-serve.d2w` — 3.80 tok/round & 227.7 t/s vs 3.47/205 with the Qwen3.8 drafter; on a 3090 fp8→use turbo5k default, fp8 KV is sm_89+ only, so on the 3090 drop `Q27_KV=fp8` and let the Ampere default apply.)\n\n## 4. Native OpenAI-compatible server\nYes — one binary, three API shapes (default bind 127.0.0.1 only; `--host 0.0.0.0 --api-key <key>` for remote; auth via `--api-key`/`--api-key-file`/`Q27_API_KEY`):\n- OpenAI: `POST /v1/chat/completions`, `POST /v1/completions` (streaming + `stream_options.include_usage`)\n- Anthropic: `POST /v1/messages` (thinking blocks, tool_use/input_json_delta, exact `count_tokens`, anthropic-shaped context-limit errors) — `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://host:8080` drives Claude Code directly\n- OpenAI Responses: `/v1/responses` (Codex-compatible)\n- `GET /health`, and `GET /metrics` (Prometheus text) behind `--enable-metrics` — per-request token counters, TTFT/E2E/ITL histograms, KV/prefix gauges, MTP accept-ratio lanes. Default port shown 8080; any `--port`.\n\n## 5. In-repo benchmark protocol/scripts (how THEY measure)\n- Methodology: `docs/BENCHMARKING.md` (39 KB). Two arms: Method A payload decode microbench (`/v1/completions`, decode-only t/s from q27's `[req]` journal line `tps=`); Method B 12 pinned SWE-bench Verified instances through Claude Code in Docker (`bench/swebench/`: `select_instances.py`, frozen `manifest.json`, `run.sh`), decode t/s from engine telemetry, wall client-side.\n- **C-ladder protocol** (`bench/crossengine/harness/ladder_tap.py`, same protocol as `bench/ladder/ladder.py` 2026-08-14): C ∈ {1,2,4,8} concurrent streams, distinct salted novel-novel prompts (no shared prefix), temp 0.6 / top-p 0.95, `max_tokens` 8192, stream=True, n=1 per point; **aggregate t/s = sum(decoded tokens) / union of per-request decode intervals** (client tap: [t_start+ttft, t_start+wall]; q27-native: reconstructed from server `[req] rid=… dec= dec_ms= tps= t=` lines, with `--calibrate` cross-check client-vs-server offset ≈ +0.0–0.1%). Legs boot with `--slots 8 --ctx 16384`. Results archived as `bench/crossengine/ladder.<leg>.txt` + `JSON {c, aggregate_tps, sum_dec, union_s, per_stream_median, ttft_ms_median, ...}`. Published 5090 ladder rows: q27 q4s 141/230/352/531 at C=1/2/4/8; Bonsai 2 T2+MTP head 173/231/384/512; ninfer NVFP4 peaks 834 at C=8. 3090-row caveat: those ladder numbers are 5090; 3090 has separate published rows (below).\n- Multislot/cache: `bench/pool/multisession.py` (cache-survival via `[req] hit=`), `tools/batch_ab.sh` (2-slot batch A/B), `bench/bonsai2/` + `tools/bench-bonsai2-8gb.sh` (small-card field report), `tools/effort_ab.sh` (agentic quality A/B with wsum gate), `bench/crossengine/` campaign readouts incl. `agentic-2026-09-18-bonsai2/`.\n\n## 6. Risk flags for 24GB / sm_86 / our campaign\n- **OOM on 24GB with default build**: the width-12 default \"OOMs at graph setup\" on 3090-class → MUST use `make build/q27-server-w8` / released `q27-server-w8`. `--ctx` auto-sizes; explicit oversized `--ctx` OOMs at spec-graph instantiation (historical: auto 36864/32768 OOM pre-recalibration; 24576 was the fp16-KV v1.4 ceiling; q4s+turbo3 = full 262,144 on 24GB, 0.67 GB spare at ready).\n- **3090 measured numbers (their box, stock ~417 W)**: 102.2 t/s median live Claude-Code decode at 131K ctx (turbo3, MTP-ladder era); club-3090 harness q4s legs: narr wall 88.5 / decode 93.2 t/s @61K ctx fp16 KV; turbo3: 89.45/94.23 narr, 108.32/117.38 code @262,144 ctx; TTFT 53–55 ms after `Q27_PF_BATCH_MIN` fix. Issue #6: a power-capped 3090 decodes at ~half the 350–420 W figure.\n- **sm_86 support**: first-class (gencode sm_86 in every engine build; `q27-server-12g` is sm_86-only; turbo5k is the Ampere default; fp8-KV/MMA paths are sm_89+/sm_120-only and never launch on sm_86). Known sm_86 perf-only niggle: `gemv_t3_n` spills 12–24 B at widths 4–8 (T3 pack + MTP ladder on 3060-class).\n- **No patched CUDA needed** — plain CUDA 12.8+ toolkit (12.8 floor due to unconditional sm_120a object; prebuilt binaries avoid this entirely and only need driver r580+ / glibc 2.38+). NixOS-relevant: static CUDA runtime in release tarballs.\n- **Weight-load corruption class**: their GPU0 silently flipped bits in ~1/3 loads (2/3 of corrupt runs still byte-identical tokens) → campaigns from 08-19 run `Q27_PRINT_WSUM=1` + wsum gate; we should do the same (each tier's expected digest is in BUILDLOG/HF cards).\n- **v0.14.4 specifically fixes** a forced-`</think>`-close bug on non-MTP Bonsai packs under a reasoning budget (solo mode streamed the whole answer as reasoning) — stock recipes pass `--think-budget 0` and were unaffected; also hardened the `.d2w` pack loader (previously a truncated pack = stack write). Pin ≥ v0.14.4 for Bonsai legs.\n- **Quality trade-off, theirs, disclosed**: Bonsai 2 measures +27% wikitext PPL (9.2508 vs 7.3121) and 25/30 HumanEval+ vs Qwen3.8 default; same SWE-bench patches landed but ~2× the turns → 2.3× wall. Qwen3.8 v2 sampler recipe is load-bearing (greedy 0.758 vs matched 0.847/0.928 suite) — always serve `--think --temp 1.0 --top-p 0.95 --top-k 20 --min-p 0.05 --think-budget 0`.\n- **DFlash2 serving is single-slot** (needs `Q27_BATCH=0`; per-slot drafter ~2.1 GB + reserve); multi-slot throughput requires the MTP-ladder path (Bonsai: `bonsai2-27b-t2-mtp.q27`, `Q27_BATCH=1`, no DFlash2). DFlash2-era cross-engine numbers are also single-slot.\n- Engine auto-selects context: on 24GB expect ~192K auto (turbo5k/q4s) or 262K with `Q27_KV=turbo3`; Bonsai 2 T2 on 24GB auto-sizes 262K-class KV comfortably.\n\nSources: README (master, 862 lines), docs/SPEC.md, docs/BENCHMARKING.md, Makefile, tools/launch_q27_38.sh, bench/crossengine/harness/ladder_tap.py, bench/crossengine/{ladder.q4s.txt,manifest.txt}, HF API for both model repos (blob sizes exact), releases v0.14.4 + commits/master.atom. [INFERENCE] none — all numbers quoted from fetched sources."
}
