euse disabled. Example: `ninfer_bench --weights qwen3_8_27b.ninfer -pg '2048,128' --spec dflash2 --draft-tokens 7 --lm-head-draft --max-ctx 4096 -r 3 --warmup 1`. `--profile-measured` brackets one repetition with cudaProfilerStart/Stop for Nsight.\n- **`tools/bench/run_chat_decode.py`**: the harness behind all headline decode numbers — syv-ai's 8 thinking-off prompts (1,024 tokens, INT8 KV, greedy) for C1/C8 decode; supports `;model=PATH` per arm, `--spec mtp|dflash2|none`, `--model-id`, `env=K=V` arm fields for A/B on one binary (controls this card's 3–5 % process-to-process drift via interleaving). 24-prompt varied-chat fixture in-repo (greedy, 512 tokens, 1 stream through ninfer-serve).\n- Op-level microbenches in one bundle: `ninfer_benches <name>` (`ninfer_linear_bench` small-T sweep `--sweep 1:128:1`, L2-flush cold sampling, CUDA-graph capture timing, `T1_lin_x` scaling metric; `ninfer_linear_topk_bench`; `ninfer_context_cost_bench` for context-cache cost-model calibration). TTFT: frozen black-box Serve fixture `bench/fixtures/ttft/` (manifest + media, does not use Engine directly).\n- Published measured numbers (3090, documented harness): DFlash2 C1 140 tok/s (vs upstream artifact 127), MTP3 C8 477 tok/s (upstream 482 — tie), C8 aggregate via `run_chat_decode`; prefill pp4096 cuBLAS 3,185 tok/s (upstream 3,196, tie); artifact card: tg128 plain 49.2, MTP3 151.5, DFlash2 261.2, 24-prompt chat DFlash2 133.5 / MTP3 115.4.\n\n## 6. Risk flags\n- **No OOM reports at 24 GB found anywhere** — this fork exists to fit 24 GB; every context figure is VRAM-measured on a 3090 (Windows defaults even sized \"beside a desktop\"; headless Linux gets the full 262K). Risk is the reverse: context caps when desktop holds VRAM (188K DFlash2 beside 1.6 GiB desktop; 196,608 refused).\n- **sm_86**: first-class target (\"native SM86 runtime\"); release archives explicitly built sm_86/CUDA 12.8 for RTX 3090. Docs warn against Ada (sm_89) flag edits.\n- **Host RAM**: `--host-state-slots 32` pins 2.34 GiB + optional host KV cache (`--host-kv-mib 8192` examples; `--auto-host-cache` sizes from machine, v0.14.0+; `--host-cache-max-mib` caps it). Weights/KV never leave GPU, but the context-cache tier is host-RAM-resident by default (32 slots, 8 shared prefixes) — for the minimize-host-RAM constraint set `NINFER_HOST_STATE_SLOTS` low / `--host-cache-max-mib` small.\n- **Patched CUDA required? No.** CUDA 12.8+ toolkit only for building; release Linux binaries need only runtime: glibc 2.38+, CUDA 12.8 runtime w/ cuBLAS, FFmpeg 6. NVFP4/K8V4 KV need Blackwell (sm_100a/sm_120a) — refused on sm_86 with explicit diagnostic (use int8/rk4v4/rk8v4).\n- Small print: spec-decode not bit-identical to greedy; long-context attention split change (41 splits) is not bit-identical and one 68.5K greedy run diverged (accepted fewer tokens, 114→100 tok/s that run); `godmode` graft drifts into Chinese ~4/6 requests on q4; DFlash2 with the 6-bit head REQUIRES `--lm-head-draft` (startup fails otherwise, also on v0.14.x); Linux archive never smoke-tested against a model by the maintainer (built/validated on Windows card; v0.15.0 release notes list Linux-binaries-against-model as \"not run\"); v0.13.0 ctest ran per-PR only; quality note: Unsloth UD-Q4_K_XL still 2× closer to Q8_0 per byte (KLD 0.0156 vs 0.0318); vision runs in overlay residency (~10 MiB device reservation) but its fallback evicts weights (lm_head/embedding/draft/MTP) during encodes.\n- MTP3 vs DFlash2 context tradeoff: DFlash2 (default) = 1 lane, MTP3 = 2 lanes at 262,144; MTP3 is the profile measured to reach the full 262,144 on Linux."
}
