th `ninfer_bench` (drives public `ninfer::Engine`): build with `-DNINFER_BUILD_BENCHMARKS=ON`, run e.g. `./build/bench/ninfer_bench --weights qwen3_8_27b.ninfer -p 512,2048 -n 128 -pg '2048,128' -r 5 --warmup 1 --kv-dtype int8 --mtp-draft-tokens 3 --lm-head-draft --no-cuda-graph -o csv`. Matrix: `pp{P}` (prefill tok/s = P/prefill_seconds), `tg{G}` (G decode tokens, G+1 convention), `pp{P}+tg{G}`; TTFT from server Engine timings. Plus op-level `ninfer_<op>_bench` (e.g. `ninfer_linear_bench --suite qwen3_6_27b`) and Nsight `--profile-measured`. README publishes measured 3090 tables: decode C1 70.19 e2e / 71.00 decode tok/s (TTFT 149 ms) → C8 161.28 e2e / 165.33 tok/s (TTFT 1,215 ms), MTP acceptance 56.8–61.1%; prefill ~844–862 tok/s aggregate at 4,362-token prompts (C8 TTFT 23 s, peak 23,207 MiB).\n\n## 6. Risk flags\n- sm_86: first-class target (hard-required `CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=86`; SM86 GDN/runtime fixes in PR #7; GeForce-safe Docker fix). Blackwell-only NVFP4/W4A4 and TMA unavailable on SM86.\n- CUDA: >= 12.8 required (release built with 12.8; flake pins 12.9 with gcc13 because nvcc 12.9 rejects GCC > 14; Docker image uses 13.1). CMake >= 3.28.\n- OOM at 24 GB: C8 prefill run peaked 23,207 MiB — tight; 35B-A3B rejected at C8 (~503 MiB over reservation); release notes: keep GPU idle during model load, use explicit KV settings for higher concurrency. Bonsai caveat above.\n- `rk8v4` KV is lossy and quality-degraded in the maintainer's own coding test (faulty nested-rollback design vs INT8) — use only when the context gain matters.\n- Design limits: one process/model/GPU, concurrency fixed at startup (1–8), bounded batching (no continuous batching), no CPU offload, no multi-GPU, tool calls returned but never executed. Host RAM stays minimal (GPU-resident weights, no offload).\n- Maturity: community/best-effort; pelian fork = synced mirror of Don-Chad master (no unique changes found) — for campaign pinning prefer parent Don-Chad/ninfer-3090 @ tag v0.6.1-rtx3090 (