TTP):\n  python3 serve_openai.py --target /models/qwen38-27b-exl3 --draft /models/dflash2-exl3 --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8889\n  Flags (argparse in container/serve_openai.py == scripts/serve_openai.py, blob b5afa9cd): --target (required), --draft (required), --host 127.0.0.1, --port 8889, --model-name qwen38-27b-exl3-dflash2, --max-model-len 262144, --cache-tokens 270336, --cq 3 (KV quant bits; cq3 = validated setting)\nChat (no server): python examples/chat.py -m models/qwen38-27b-exl3 -mode chatml -dm models/dflash2-exl3 -cs 262144 -cq 3\nKey flags summary: max-context = -cs 262144 / --max-model-len 262144 / CTX=262144 env; concurrency = 1 sequence slot only (Cache max_batch_size=1, FIFO single worker; at 262k only one sequence fits); spec-decode = draft via -dm/--draft (native DFlash2, draft window default_draft_size=4, GDN rewind); quant/artifact selection = -b/--cq cache bits + quant dir choice.\n3090 env knobs (defaults, don't override): EXL3_HGEMM_F16ACC=auto (2.00x on sm_86), EXL3_INT8_GEMV=2, EXL3_INT8_GEMV_MAX_K=5, EXL3_QC_STAGING=1.\n\n## 3. Model artifacts (HF, both public, lastModified 2026-09-17)\n- Target: r0b0tlab/Qwen3.8-27B-EXL3-4.00bpw (arch qwen3_5 Qwen3_5ForConditionalGeneration, image-text-to-text; base Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B; quantization_config quant_method=exl3 bits=4). Files: model-00001-of-00002.safetensors + model-00002-of-00002.safetensors + model.safetensors.index.json, chat_template.jinja, tokenizer.json, preprocessor/video_preprocessor_config, crc32.txt. On-disk size 15.4 GiB (HF usedStorage 16,522,370,618 bytes ~= 15.4 GiB incl misc). Conversion recipe: convert.py -i <bf16> -o <dir> -w <work> -b 4.00 -vb 6 -mb 4 -hb 6 (4.00bpw decoder, 6bpw lm_head, 6bpw vision, 4bpw native MTP head).\n- Draft: r0b0tlab/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2-EXL3-4.00bpw (arch DFlash2DraftModel, model_type qwen3; base incoai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2; exl3 bits=4). Single model.safetensors; 1.2 GiB (usedStorage 1,254,647,206 bytes). conv/selector kept fp16.\n- BF16 sources (conversion only): 48.4 GiB + 3.4 GiB.\n- FIT on 24 GB WITHOUT CPU offload at 262,144 ctx: YES — measured, single sequence: weights ~15.5 + 1.2 GiB; KV cq3 (3-bit, 16 full-attn layers x 4 kv heads x 256 dim x 2) = 3.0 GiB at 262k; GDN verify history ~1.22 GiB; staging+CUDA ctx ~2.5 GiB. Reported: 21.7 GB loaded idle, 20.7 GiB mean serving, 22.7 GiB nvidia-smi peak, 23.13 GB torch peak during 150k prefill+decode. GPU-resident only, no host offload path involved.\n\n## 4. Native OpenAI-compatible server: YES (minimal)\nserve_openai.py (stdlib http.server, port default 8889):\n- GET /health, GET /v1/health; GET /v1/models (reports max_model_len 262144)\n- POST /v1/chat/completions (NON-streaming only; stream:true -> 400 \"streaming not implemented\"; honors chat_template_kwargs; splits </think> into reasoning_content)\n- POST /v1/chat/completions/render (exact chat-template token ids)\n- POST /v1/completions (raw prompt string or token-id list)\nFIFO single worker thread, max_batch_size=1 — concurrent requests queue serially, no parallel batching. Also examples/chat.py interactive entrypoint. (The sibling GB10 kit uses TabbyAPI for OpenAI serve; for this 3090 kit the OpenAI surface is serve_openai.py.)\n\n## 5. In-repo benchmark protocol/scripts (scripts/)\n- acceptance_check.py — GSM8K greedy n=40, acceptance length + decode tok/s; gate: acceptance >= 4.0 and > MTP+0.3. Result: 5.657 acceptance, 162.9 tok/s DFlash2 (vs 116.3 MTP head, 42.8 AR).\n- long_context_check.py — 262k-context load + 150k prefill + decode: 594 tok/s prefill, 25.3 tok/s decode @150k, 23.13 GB peak.\n- sampled_sanity_check.py — T=1.0 sampled distribution sanity (notes/LOSSLESS.md).\n- concurrency_check.py — ladder 1/2/4; artifacts metrics/concurrency/ladder-1-2.json, ladder-1-2-4.json. 4 concurrent seqs @1024 tok/slot = 19.5 GiB.\n- niah_multikey.py — multi-needle NIAH at 262,080 tokens via container serve: PASS 2n 613.8 s, PASS 3n 122.8 s (prefix reuse).\n- vram_budget.py (VRAM budget gate), sample_telemetry.sh (nvidia-smi 2 s cadence -> metrics/*/telemetry.tsv), check_dflash2_history_guard.py.\n- Tok/s measurement: decode tok/s from generator job (elapsed + completion_tokens; server returns elapsed in result; E2E harness numbers in commit 3ac4be9: 152.82/159.29/144.73 tok/s across Q200v2 runs). TTFT: not a first-class metric in these scripts; prefill tok/s and long-context depth benchmarks instead.\n\n## 6. Risk flags\n- sm_86: explicitly supported and 3090-native — Dockerfile compiles ext for TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=8.6 in-image (host-built .so would fail GLIBC_2.43); ENV.md documents sm_86 tuning (EXL3_HGEMM_F16ACC=auto measured 2.00x on sm_86; Ampere int8 GEMV cap K=5). No patched CUDA needed beyond CUDA 13 toolkit (torch 2.10.0+cu130, libcudart.so.13 on LD_LIBRARY_PATH; their driver 595.84).\n- VRAM: full 262k ctx is SINGLE-sequence only; 23.13 GB peak leaves ~0.9 GB headroom — any extra concurrent sequence at depth will OOM. Concurrency >1 only at short contexts. cache_tokens 270336 (262144+8192 headroom) is the default; do not raise.\n- No streaming endpoint; quality graders must use non-streaming.\n- Engine is a fork pin (community@355c6ee), not upstream: DFlash2 native CUDA + GDN rewind + dense M=32/64 TILEBLOCKS_M live only there; kit explicitly forbids overlaying the old patches/ (dflash2-pathway) onto the v1.5.0 wheel; published drafts need 355c6ee codebook-key fallback (*.weight vs native codebook). Upstream moved to v1.6.0 without these.\n- Docker host needs libcuda bind (-v /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libcuda.so.1:...:ro + libnvidia-ml.so.1 + TRITON_LIBCUDA_PATH) per container/run-serve.sh; no nvidia-container-toolkit needed.\n- OOM reports: kit has 0 open issues; no OOM issue reports found in kit repo. Upstream turboderp issue search was rate-limited (HTTP 403) during this scout, so upstream-wide OOM reports not exhaustively checked [INFERENCE: none observed, not proven absent globally].\n- Model quirk: target quant is qwen3_5 arch with vision tower; its chat template raises \"No user query found in messages.\" when the last message isn't a real user query — same upstream template family implicated in the user's earlier oh-my-pi 500 loop (ollama qwen3.8:27b); any agent harness against this server must always send a trailing user message.\n- NixOS note: container path (docker/podman with device binds) is the lowest-friction route; host build needs CUDA 13 toolkit."
}
