{
  "cand-scout#8": "CANDIDATE: trellis-serve (sglang-exl3 plugin) — EXL3 3.0bpw Qwen3.8-27B on RTX 3090 (sm_86), MTP + DFlash2\n\n## 1. Repo, release/tag, commit-ish\n- Repo: https://github.com/0xSero/trellis-serve — redirects to **sybil-solutions/trellis-serve** (org transfer; both URLs valid). NOT-FOUND is false: repo exists, active (PR #4 merged ~2026-10-06, updated_time 1791369731 unix ≈ 2026-10-06).\n- License MIT, Python. Monorepo: `core/` (trellis_core format reader + bit-exact torch reference), `cuda/` (sglang_exl3 plugin + Marlin-template EXL3 kernels for sm_86), `xpu/` (Intel Arc B70, irrelevant here).\n- **No git tags, no GitHub releases** (releases.atom and tags.atom both empty). Release channel = container images: `ghcr.io/0xsero/sglang-exl3:v0.7.0-ampere@sha256:c8922bd7256caf1b273af7ac49221e652be9e6072c1cdec4b959f506fd415d79` (attested, digest-pinned in the validated recipes).\n- Commit-ish for a source build: `main` @ `c7c883729d72db9220d1085015798ab490609d7c` (latest); long-context/vision work also lives on branch `flashnext-phase-d` @ `b1e74af` (per local-ai-images README; Phase D = 5-bit QSA KV, expert-cache reserve, 12k prefill chunks — for the 85 GB Flash-Next model, not needed for the 27B).\n- Engine pins: SGLang **v0.5.20** + ExLlamaV3 **v1.5.1** (plugin = no SGLang source edits; registers `--quantization exl3` via `sglang.srt.plugins` entry point).\n\n## 2. Build / serve invocation (exact)\nPublished-image path (validated, recommended):\n```bash\ndocker pull ghcr.io/0xsero/sglang-exl3:v0.7.0-ampere@sha256:c8922bd7256caf1b273af7ac49221e652be9e6072c1cdec4b959f506fd415d79\n# boot exactly as the recipe does:\ncuda/scripts/smoke_published.sh <digest> turboderp-Qwen3.8-27B-exl3-3.00bpw run1 <launch args below>\n```\nSource path:\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/0xSero/trellis-serve && cd trellis-serve\ndocker build -f cuda/docker/Dockerfile.dev -t sglang-exl3:dev .        # ARG BASE=lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.20, EXLLAMAV3_TAG=v1.5.1, TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=8.6\ndocker run --rm --gpus device=0 -v $PWD:/opt/trellis-serve -w /opt/trellis-serve/cuda/csrc --entrypoint bash sglang-exl3:dev -c ./build.sh\ncuda/scripts/serve_3090.sh turboderp-Qwen3.8-27B-exl3-3.00bpw run1 --quantization exl3 ...   # model dir must be under ~/models (mounted ro at /models)\n```\n`served-serve` inner command (serve_3090.sh): `python3 -m sglang.launch_server --model-path /models/$MODEL --quantization exl3 --trust-remote-code --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT --served-model-name $MODEL` + extra args; `PYTHONPATH=/opt/sglang-exl3/csrc/build/lib`, `SGLANG_EXL3_MODEL_PATH=/models/$MODEL`, forwards all `SGLANG_*`/`PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF` env, publishes 127.0.0.1:$PORT (default 30000), `HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1`.\n\nValidated launch args (accepted C1 recipe `qwen38-27b-exl3-3bpw-mtp-vision-rtx3090-sglang-tp1`, 2026-09-26):\n```\n--context-length 212992 --mem-fraction-static 0.82 --kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3\n--mamba-ssm-dtype bfloat16 --max-running-requests 1 --max-mamba-cache-size 3\n--cuda-graph-max-bs-decode 1 --cuda-graph-max-bs-prefill 240\n--chunked-prefill-size 4096 --max-prefill-tokens 4096 --prefill-decode-interval 16\n--reasoning-parser qwen3 --tool-call-parser qwen3_coder\n--mamba-radix-cache-strategy no_buffer --disable-overlap-schedule --image-processor-backend pil\n--speculative-algorithm NEXTN --speculative-num-steps 3 --speculative-eagle-topk 1 --speculative-num-draft-tokens 4\n--speculative-token-map /opt/sglang-exl3/tokenmaps/qwen38_hot32k_v2.pt\n```\nEnv: `PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True`, `SGLANG_EXL3_EMBED_HOST=1`, `SGLANG_EXL3_PREFILL_FP16_ACC=1`, `SGLANG_EXL3_VIT_MLP_CHUNK=8192`, `SGLANG_EXL3_VIT_SDPA=1`, `SGLANG_OPT_MAMBA_SKIP_DECODE_LOCK=1`, `SGLANG_VLM_CACHE_SIZE_MB=256`.\n- **Max-context flag**: `--context-length` (validated 212,992 C1 / 172,032 C4; native 262,144).\n- **Concurrency**: `--max-running-requests` + `--cuda-graph-max-bs-decode` + `--max-mamba-cache-size` (C4 variant: 4 / 4 / 12, mem-fraction 0.83).\n- **Spec-decode**: MTP = `--speculative-algorithm NEXTN 3/1/4` (draft head inside checkpoint, no extra download) + optional FR-Spec `--speculative-token-map`. DFlash2 = `--speculative-algorithm DFLASH --speculative-draft-model-path <dir>` (SGLang upstream algorithm; the plugin's `Exl3Config.from_config` explicitly supports EXL3 **draft** checkpoints carrying their own manifest — a DFlash2 EXL3 draft dir works as the draft path).\n- **Quant/artifact selection**: `--model-path` points at any EXL3 branch (3.00bpw / SC_3.00bpw_H4 etc.); kernel choice via `SGLANG_EXL3_KERNEL=auto|marlin|exllamav3` (auto = Marlin-template sm_86 kernels, bit-identical decode to exllamav3_ext.reconstruct; prefill ≥144 rows reconstructs fp16 slices → cuBLAS). Other knobs: `SGLANG_EXL3_KEEP_TRELLIS=0` (24 GB layout: only repacked trellis resident), `SGLANG_EXL3_DENSE_ROWS=144`, `SGLANG_EXL3_DENSE_SLICE_MB=64`, `SGLANG_EXL3_PAD_SMALL_M=1`.\n- Caveat: `--speculative-token-map` file `/opt/sglang-exl3/tokenmaps/qwen38_hot32k_v2.pt` is baked into the published image; for a from-source build the mounted tree must contain it (or drop the flag — pure MTP works without it).\n\n## 3. Model artifacts\n- **Qwen3.8-27B EXL3 3.0bpw**: HF repo **`turboderp/Qwen3.8-27B-exl3`, branch `3.00bpw`** (validated rev `6fe61ad6`). Files: `model-00001-of-00002.safetensors` = 8,575,532,487 B, `model-00002-of-00002.safetensors` = 5,244,406,822 B → **13,819,939,309 B ≈ 12.87 GiB weights**, plus `tokenizer.json` (12.8 MB), `quantization_config.json` (629 KB), `chat_template.jinja`. Download: `huggingface-cli download turboderp/Qwen3.8-27B-exl3 --revision 3.00bpw --local-dir turboderp-Qwen3.8-27B-exl3-3.00bpw`. (Self-calibrated `SC_3.00bpw_H4` branch exists, same size class, likely better quality; recipes used plain 3.00bpw.)\n- **DFlash2 draft**: **`Mia-AiLab/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2-EXL3-5.0bpw`** — `model.safetensors` = 1,470,916,078 B ≈ **1.37 GiB** (+ config.json/quantization_config.json). Same weights published by MiaAI-Lab GitHub org kit.\n- **Fits 24 GB without weight/KV CPU offload**: YES for ≤209k context — measured peak 22,628 MiB (94% of 24,576) at C1/212,992 with vision; 22,852 MiB (93%) at C4/172,032; KV pool 219,025 tokens (fp8 KV) at C1. **262,144 tokens: NOT validated** — the coherence ladder tops out at a 208,858-token prompt. [INFERENCE] 262k fp8-KV at C1 plausibly fits only with mem-fraction ≈0.86–0.88 and no vision load, since pool scales with the freed fraction, but no recipe proves it; expect to trade the vision/256 MB cache or a few GiB of headroom. Caveat: the validated recipe sets `SGLANG_EXL3_EMBED_HOST=1` — the embedding table is kept in host RAM (bounded, with a 256 MB GPU cache). If the campaign forbids ANY host-resident weights, set `SGLANG_EXL3_EMBED_HOST=0` and pay ~2–2.5 GB VRAM (context shrinks accordingly). Excluding that knob, weights/KV are GPU-resident only.\n- **Ternary Bonsai 2 27B**: **NOT-FOUND as EXL3/trellis** — HF API search `Bonsai exl3` and `author=turboderp Bonsai` both return `[]`; turboderp has no Bonsai EXL3. Per 0xSero's local-ai-images README, Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B exists only as Prism-ML `PTQ1_0`/`PQ2_0` ternary packings loadable **only by Prism's llama.cpp fork** (stock llama.cpp rejects the types) — a different engine, not servable by trellis-serve. Do not pair Bonsai 2 with this candidate.\n\n## 4. Native OpenAI-compatible server\nYes — stock SGLang 0.5.20: port 30000 (recipe-pinned), endpoints `/v1/chat/completions` (streaming + tools via `qwen3_coder` tool parser; reasoning via `qwen3` parser → `reasoning_content`), `/v1/completions`, `/v1/models`. Chat only (SGLang has no native Anthropic/Responses API), but 0xSero's registry ships a `gateway` image that fronts the engine: OpenAI chat passthrough + Anthropic Messages + OpenAI Responses translation, streaming and tool calls included, share-key enforced.\n\n## 5. In-repo benchmark protocol / scripts\n- `cuda/scripts/smoke_published.sh` — boots the published digest exactly as the registry recipe (argv shim, per-model mounts, env forwarding) for reproducible runs.\n- `cuda/scripts/serve_3090.sh` — dev-image serve wrapper; writes `serve_cmd.txt`, `engine.log`, `container_id.txt` per run.\n- `cuda/src/sglang_exl3/tools/`: `decode_microbench.py`, `marlin_microbench.py`, `moe_inspect.py`, `moe_parity_sm86.py` — kernel-level decode tok/s microbenches + parity checks.\n- `xpu/bench/`: `accept_probe.py` (spec-decode acceptance-rate probing), `attn_bench.py`, `fetch_corpus.sh`, `filter_replay_corpus.py`.\n- How THEY measure (registry harness `rtx-3090/bench/harness.py`, referenced from recipes): coherence ladder (prompt 1k→209k, TTFT per level), panel (per-stream decode tok/s, prose vs code prompts, 3 waves, T0 and T0.7, thinking on/off), 10-minute soak (throughput drift %, TTFT p95). Published numbers: C1 prose 96.2 / code 141.1 tok/s (32k-prompt: 84.0/118.4); C4 aggregate 274.9/408.7; cold prefill 1.5–1.7k tok/s to 32k, 927 @131k, 710 @209k; AWQ-INT4 no-spec baseline 45 tok/s.\n- `docs/lossless-check.md` — bit-exactness verification of kernel decode vs ExLlamaV3.\n\n## 6. Risk flags\n- **VRAM/OOM at 24 GB**: validated at 94% peak (C1/209k+vision); 4096² images OOM'd with prefill CUDA graphs >240 tokens (fixed by cap: 0.49 GB graphs); C4/32K soak passes but \"the C4 cells at 32K cannot hold four decoding streams on this card\" (gate-7 failures: LOOP, STREAM_ENDED, UNDERFILLED; greedy 10k long-form loops). C4 is a rejected candidate recipe, C1 is accepted.\n- **262k not proven**: validated window tops at 209k (C1); 262k needs mem-fraction/feature trade-offs, unvalidated.\n- **`SGLANG_EXL3_EMBED_HOST=1`** in the validated recipe = embedding table in host RAM (see §3) — conflicts with a strict GPU-resident-only reading unless disabled.\n- **sm_86**: first-class target (Marlin-template EXL3 kernels compiled `TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=8.6`, min capability 80, all tuning done on bare RTX 3090). Upstream ExLlamaV3's own kernels have a sm_86 red flag (issue #291 \"Illegal memory access in coop_autotune.cu:464 on RTX 3090, Qwen3.8-27B EXL3 4.5bpw\"; issue #144 Ampere perf) — this repo's default `SGLANG_EXL3_KERNEL=marlin` avoids the exllamav3_ext decode path; the exllamav3_ext kernel remains only as bit-parity reference (and `SGLANG_EXL3_MARLIN_MAX_N=65536` sends wider layers to it — worth overriding to keep everything on Marlin).\n- **Patched CUDA**: none required beyond the pinned image (SGLang v0.5.20 + exllamav3 v1.5.1 built AOT for sm_86); no driver tricks, standard Docker + NVIDIA toolkit.\n- **DFlash2 on this stack is the unproven leg**: trellis-serve has no DFlash2-specific code or measured numbers; its MTP numbers (96.2/141.1 tok/s) are the validated spec-decode mode. DFlash2 depends on SGLang's `DFLASH` algorithm (documented upstream; DFlash2 needs SGLang PR #35371 — inclusion in v0.5.20 unverified) + the plugin's EXL3 draft-checkpoint loading (which does exist in `config.py`). The DFlash2 artifact is real (Mia-AiLab, 1.37 GiB) but its published numbers (DGX Spark, ~34.5 tok/s, +33% vs MTP) come from the MiaAI exllamav3 fork, not from SGLang/trellis-serve. Budget for a bring-up experiment, not a guaranteed recipe.\n- **Maturity**: 2 stars, 3 open-but-zero issues shown, single-author project; mitigations = digest-pinned attested image + published recipe JSONs with full evidence (ladder/soak/tuning ledger).\n- Provenance for the accepted image: `gh attestation verify oci://ghcr.io/0xsero/sglang-exl3@sha256:c8922bd7... -o 0xSero`; build workflow run 36210770340 (2026-09-26)."
