  "cand-scout#9": "CANDIDATE: moki1/qwen38-27b-rtx3090test — patched vLLM 0.27.1 stack serving Qwen3.8-27B (hybrid GatedDeltaNet+attention, 27.78B) on one RTX 3090 (24 GB, sm86). All fields verified from live GitHub raw/API fetches 2026-10-08.\n\n1. REPO / VERSION\n- URL: https://github.com/moki1/qwen38-27b-rtx3090test (Apache-2.0)\n- It is a FORK of syv-ai/qwen38-27b-rtx3090, which upstream renamed syv-ai/HyperQwen (1.9k stars, actively developed, last push 2026-10-08; HEAD tree 10bb488418064b50738c925b70c9510785c3c949).\n- Fork HEAD: commit 51905d1902e699e35e4c11cb0eb9ffe230a11344 (\"Drop the demo caption…\", 2026-08-20T20:38:09Z, author mhenrichsen/mads@syv.ai). Fork is a FROZEN snapshot — created 2026-08-21, zero stars, issues disabled, pushed_at 2026-08-20. No tags (tags API: []); releases endpoint 403, no release assets known [INFERENCE: none, repo has no release infra]. No releases/tags/CHANGES — versioning is git-commit-only.\n- Pinned stack (docker/requirements.txt): vllm==0.27.1 (pins torch 2.13.0+cu130, triton 3.7.1, flashinfer-python 0.6.16.post3), transformers==5.15.0, tokenizers==0.22.2, compressed-tensors==0.17.0, huggingface_hub==1.27.0, hf_transfer==0.1.9, ninja==1.13.0. Python 3.12. ~40 GB disk.\n\n2. BUILD / SERVE (exact)\nSetup (venv path, from README):\n```\ngit clone https://github.com/moki1/qwen38-27b-rtx3090test ~/qwen-serving && cd ~/qwen-serving\npython3 -m venv venv\nvenv/bin/pip install vllm huggingface_hub hf_transfer ninja\nHF_HUB_ENABLE_HF_TRANSFER=1 venv/bin/hf download dbirks/Qwen3.8-27B-W4A16-AutoRound --local-dir models/Qwen3.8-27B-W4A16-AutoRound\nvenv/bin/python prepare/quant_lm_head.py models/Qwen3.8-27B-W4A16-AutoRound   # lm_head -> int8 (releases 2.6 GB KV pages)\nvenv/bin/python prepare/quant_embed.py   models/Qwen3.8-27B-W4A16-AutoRound  # embed_tokens -> int8\nvenv/bin/python prepare/quant_mtp.py     models/Qwen3.8-27B-W4A16-AutoRound  # MTP draft module -> int4 GPTQ (850->215 MB)\nvenv/bin/python prepare/build_draft_vocab.py models/Qwen3.8-27B-W4A16-AutoRound --ids prepare/draft_vocab_ids.json  # 40k-token draft head\nvenv/bin/python prepare/fetch_fast_variant.py    # optional fast variant, ~1 GB from syvai/qwen3.8-27b-3090-fast-variant\nvenv/bin/python prepare/fetch_dflash2.py         # optional DFlash2 drafter 1.2 GB\nfor p in patches/*.patch; do patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < $p; done\nbash kvarn/install.sh   # optional KVarN 4/2-bit KV port for 262k\nopenssl rand -hex 24 > api_key.txt\nbash verify.sh --no-server   # checks vllm 0.27.1, every patch applied, requant done\n```\nPATCHES TO APPLY (15, all written against vLLM 0.27.1, dir patches/): _check_applied.py (checker), dflash2-backport.patch, dflash2-lookup-drafting.patch, hybrid-kv-groups-v2-cudagraph.patch, hybrid-sw-block-promote.patch, marlin-int8-layer-select.patch, marlin-int8-negative-scales.patch, qwen3_5-embed-quant.patch, qwen3_5-mtp-draft-vocab.patch, sampler-small-topk-fast-softmax.patch, spec-decode-attn.patch, spec-decode-int8-kv.patch, speed-knobs-envs.patch, vllm-pr50021-gdn-spec-bounds.patch. Optional extra: kvarn/kvarn-0.27.1.patch (KVarN KV backend). Reapply after any vLLM upgrade. There is also Docker: `docker compose --profile single up -d` (or --profile batch), image builds venv+patches+model+requant, API on port 18020.\n\nSERVE FLAGS — batch/throughput mode (`bash batch/start_qwen.sh`; ~942 e2e / ~1094 steady tok/s @C64, 150k ctx):\n```\nvenv/bin/vllm serve models/Qwen3.8-27B-W4A16-AutoRound \\\n  --served-model-name qwen3.8-27b --host 0.0.0.0 --port 18020 \\\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.972 --max-model-len 150000 --max-num-seqs 64 \\\n  --api-server-count 1 --language-model-only \\\n  --kv-cache-dtype fp8 --mamba-ssm-cache-dtype float16 \\\n  --async-scheduling --max-num-batched-tokens 2048 \\\n  --compilation-config '{\"max_cudagraph_capture_size\":64,\"custom_ops\":[\"+rms_norm\",\"+silu_and_mul\"]}' \\\n  --reasoning-parser qwen3\n# env: VLLM_MARLIN_INPUT_DTYPE=int8 (W4A8 int8-tensor-core MLP GEMMs; INT8_LAYERS=gate_up gentler; INT8_LAYERS=. needs GPU_UTIL=0.95, +11%)\n#      VLLM_MARLIN_INT8_INCLUDE_RE=mlp ; VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER=0\n#      PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True (NOT optional)\n# PREFIX_CACHE=1 -> adds --enable-prefix-caching --mamba-cache-mode align\n# KV=kvarn -> --kv-cache-dtype kvarn_k4v2_g128 --block-size 128, MAX_LEN=262144, GPU_UTIL=0.93, KVARN_POOL_MEM_FRAC=0.25\n# KV=int4pth -> --kv-cache-dtype int4_per_token_head --attention-backend TRITON_ATTN, MAX_LEN=262144\n```\nSERVE FLAGS — single-user/latency mode (`bash single-user/start_qwen.sh`; ~114 tok/s default / ~124 greedy @C1, MTP; ~122/132 DFlash2):\n```\nvenv/bin/vllm serve models/Qwen3.8-27B-W4A16-AutoRound-fast \\\n  --served-model-name qwen3.8-27b --port 18020 \\\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.93 --max-model-len 65536 --max-num-seqs 8 \\\n  --api-server-count 1 --language-model-only \\\n  --attention-backend FLASH_ATTN --kv-cache-dtype bfloat16 \\\n  --mamba-ssm-cache-dtype float16 --async-scheduling --max-num-batched-tokens 2048 \\\n  --speculative-config '{\"method\":\"mtp\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":4,\"draft_sample_method\":\"probabilistic\"}' \\\n  --compilation-config '{\"max_cudagraph_capture_size\":32,\"custom_ops\":[\"+rms_norm\",\"+silu_and_mul\"]}' \\\n  --reasoning-parser qwen3\n# CTX=fast (default): 64k ctx, 4 drafts, bf16 KV, FLASH_ATTN; VLLM_SPEC_DECODE_ATTN=1 (split-KV verify Triton kernel)\n# CTX=long: 150k ctx, 3 drafts, fp8 KV via FlashInfer (k=4 crashes on FlashInfer 0.27.1)\n# CTX=huge: KVarN, 200k ctx with MTP\n# SPEC=dflash2 DFLASH_TOKENS=15 PREFIX_CACHE=1: '{\"method\":\"dflash\",\"model\":\"models/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2-W4A16\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":15}',\n#   7 drafts in one non-AR pass + context-lookup drafting (VLLM_DFLASH2_LOOKUP=1), 381-382 tok/s reproducing 25k ctx;\n#   pins --kv-cache-memory 5583457484 (5.2 GiB) and VLLM_V2_CUDAGRAPH_MEM_MIB, drops to 4 slots/56k ctx at k=15\n```\nConcurrency knob: --max-num-seqs (64 batch default; MAX_SEQS env). Spec-decode mode knob: --speculative-config JSON (method mtp|dflash, num_speculative_tokens, draft_sample_method). Quant/artifact selection: MODEL env var (base vs -fast variant), KV env var, INT8_ACT/INT8_LAYERS env vars.\n\n3. MODEL ARTIFACTS\n- Main: HF `dbirks/Qwen3.8-27B-W4A16-AutoRound` — int4 W4A16 (gs128, symmetric) compressed-tensors/AutoRound of Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B; ~19.5 GB on disk (7 safetensors shards), 49K downloads. Vision tower + mtp + lm_head kept BF16 in the published artifact; repo's prepare/ scripts then requantize lm_head+embed to int8 and MTP to int4-GPTQ in-place. Marlin int4 kernel, \"any Ampere-or-newer\", no Blackwell needed. Quant quality: GSM8K 0.917 vs 0.911 BF16, HumanEval 0.957 vs 0.939, MMLU-Pro 0.826 vs 0.819.\n- Fast variant (single-user): `syvai/qwen3.8-27b-3090-fast-variant` ~1 GB (shard 7 + model_extra_tensors.safetensors + mtp_draft_vocab_ids.pt), assembled via prepare/fetch_fast_variant.py into models/Qwen3.8-27B-W4A16-AutoRound-fast (hardlinks shards 1-6 from base).\n- DFlash2 drafter: `syvai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2-W4A16` 1.2 GB (requant of bf16 `incoai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2` 3.85 GB) via prepare/fetch_dflash2.py.\n- 24 GB FIT — VERIFIED GPU-RESIDENT, NO CPU OFFLOAD, at multiple contexts: fp8 KV batch mode = 150k ctx shipped max (~205-225k-token pool, ~195k ceiling; peak VRAM 23.0 GiB @C8). 262k full context fits ONLY with a smaller KV: KVarN k4v2 (420k-token pool @4 slots, needle correct at 240k) or vLLM built-in `int4_per_token_head` on TRITON_ATTN (355k pool, 262k fits, needle 240k ok) — both documented and zero-CPU-offload; plain fp8 cannot reach 262k (2 KB/token/16 attn layers). Host RAM: weights load from disk to GPU; requant steps are CPU-only; no offload path anywhere in scripts. Docker/WSL2 reproduction documented (docs/docker.md).\n\n4. OpenAI-COMPATIBLE SERVER: yes, native vLLM OpenAI server, port 18020 (PORT env). Endpoints: /v1/chat/completions (served-model-name `qwen3.8-27b`, Bearer key auth from api_key.txt/VLLM_API_KEY, reasoning-parser qwen3, chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking), /v1/completions, /health, /metrics (Prometheus; bench script scrapes vllm:spec_decode_num_drafts/accepted_tokens). Also `vllm bench serve` drives the same API.\n\n5. IN-REPO BENCHMARK PROTOCOL: `bash bench/run_benchmarks.sh batch|single [--prefill] [--long]` — wraps `vllm bench serve` against the live server. Measures: output tok/s (e2e), decode = C×1000/mean-TPOT and C×1000/median-TPOT, mean TTFT, median ITL, tokens/step via Prometheus spec-decode counters. Cohorts C1/C2/C4/C8 with 8 realistic chat prompts (bench/prompts_real.jsonl, 1024 out, model-default T and greedy) + 64-concurrent random 128in/512out and 256/256 rows; prefill matrix 1k→100k; long rows 1×100k, 4×60k. Warmup + run-twice rules documented (first run reads 30-50% low). Quality: bench/quality_battery.py (perplexity + GSM8K live), docs/quality.md (IFBench 78.3 vs 79.5 unquant, PPL 8.09). Also labd_bench.py/labd_accept.py/labd_soak.py for spec-decode; their protocol deliberately contrasts with ninfer-3090's random-token cohorts (they argue random tokens break spec-decode acceptance).\n\n6. RISK FLAGS\n- sm86/3090 explicitly supported and the whole repo targets it; README numbers measured ON a 3090 at 250 W. fp8_per_token_head KV does NOT start on sm86 (Triton fp8 needs SM89+) — avoid that mode.\n- OOM at 24 GB: many documented and solved cases — expandable_segments:True mandatory (DeltaNet prefill workspace fragments allocator; OOM at util>=0.975 without); MTP mode must run GPU_UTIL=0.93 (spec-decode DeltaNet workspace exceeds startup profile; dies mid-request at 0.95+); INT8_LAYERS=. needs GPU_UTIL=0.95 (OOM in chunk_fwd_o ~17 requests at 0.972); prompt_logprobs OOMs at 0.972; TurboQuant 4-bit KV (`turboquant_4bit_nc`) OOMs at 32k+ prompts on this card (chunked-prefill scratch) — KVarN instead; V2 runner CUDA-graph memory must be reserved (VLLM_V2_CUDAGRAPH_MEM_MIB) or dies on first prefill.\n- Patched CUDA / patched vLLM: 15 patches against vLLM 0.27.1 ONLY (verify.sh warns otherwise); flashinfer sampler disabled via VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER=0 for old system nvcc (attention kernels JIT fine); Triton/FlashInfer JIT warmup on first start; KVarN is a port of a vLLM 0.23 fork.\n- FlashInfer k=4 draft crash: illegal memory access on vLLM 0.27.1 FlashInfer backend when one request finishes while another is mid-gen (CTX=long drafts 3; club-3090 reports same \"n=4 dies, n=3 stable\").\n- Operational traps: stale/dirty-GPU restart silently loses ~25% (units gate on free VRAM); torch.compile cache vs env-var changes (KeyError input_global_scale; VLLM_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE=1 escape); model path containing \"dflash\" misroutes spec method; rsync mtime/.pyc staleness; quality battery mandatory before trusting throughput (int8 path once emitted garbage).\n- Fitness as a comparable candidate: it is a vLLM-0.27.1+requant+spec-decode stack, not a stock engine; benchmarking it fairly means running their start scripts + their verify.sh, and their own numbers (C1 ~45 batch / ~114-124 single-user MTP / 122-132 DFlash2; C64 ~1094; prefill 1810 @1k, ~1000 @100k; TTFT ~100 s for 100k) come from their own real-prompt protocol. NOTE: this fork is 7 weeks stale vs upstream syv-ai/HyperQwen (patch set and numbers may have moved upstream); for a current snapshot consider upstream, but the fork commit 51905d19 is exactly what was asked."
