ntext and can OOM), `-np N` concurrency slots (KV per slot multiplies), `-ngl 99` full offload, `-fa on` required for quantized KV (build may need `-DGGML_CUDA_FA_ALL_QUANTS=ON` for quantized-KV+FA), `-ctk/-ctv` KV quant, `--jinja` needed for native tool_calls on 27B, `--reasoning-budget N` caps server-wide thinking (27B reasons by default; `reasoning_effort: \"high\"` returns HTTP 500 — use `xhigh` default or `medium`; `low` unsupported).\n- Demo wrapper equivalent: `BONSAI_CTX=262144 ./scripts/start_llama_server.sh` (BONSAI_CTX up to 262144; auto `-ngl` on GPU; RAM-tiered default context otherwise). Single-user smoothness flag from maintainers: `-np 1 --cache-ram 24576` (prompt-cache too small for long conversations otherwise, Bonsai-demo#183).\n- Spec-decode: **Bonsai 2 27B has NO official drafter** — `BONSAI_SPECULATIVE=1` warns and runs plain for the bonsai2 family. The dspark drafter exists only for previous-gen Ternary-Bonsai-27B (Q2_0): convert `Ternary-Bonsai-27B-dspark-bf16.gguf` via `gguf-dspark-to-dflash` + `llama-quantize ... Q4_0` (name must contain `dspark-dflash`), then `-md <drafter> --spec-type draft-dspark --spec-draft-n-max 4 -ngld 999 -np 1` (1.8–2.4× decode on L40S-class CUDA, code/math best). Also `--spec-type ngram-*` is a no-op on these files (#203). So for Bonsai 2 27B the spec-decode mode = none available officially.\n\n3. ARTIFACTS (HF `prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-gguf`, repo rev b072e1d3b35a0a630cece372c2127528e0994386, updated 2026-09-25)\n- `Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-PTQ1_0.gguf` — 5.95 GB, 1.75–1.76 bpw (smaller; faster decode on Ada; recommended footprint pick)\n- `Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-PQ2_0.gguf` — 7.21 GB, 2.13 bpw (faster prompt processing; demo default; on CUDA both fine)\n- Vision (optional): `Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-mmproj-Q8_0.gguf` 629 MB / `mmproj-BF16.gguf` 931 MB (`BONSAI_MMPROJ_CPU=1` keeps it in RAM, ~0.9 GiB VRAM back)\n- Download: `hf download prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-gguf --include \"*PTQ1_0*\" --local-dir models` (add `--include \"*mmproj*\"` only if vision needed)\n- 27.36B params (24.35B lang + 0.47B vision + 2.54B embed/head); hybrid attention ~75% linear (Gated DeltaNet) / ~25% full → KV = 64 KiB/token F16 (16 full-attn layers × 4 KV heads × 256 dim).\n\n4. 24GB VRAM FIT (GPU-resident, no CPU offload)\n- KV F16 = 64 KiB/tok → 262,144 tok = 16 GiB.\n- PTQ1_0 @ 262K: 5.95 + 16.0 + ~0.8–1.2 compute buffers ≈ 22.8–23.2 GB → borderline fit on 24576 MiB (needs `-fa on`, no mmproj in VRAM or `BONSAI_MMPROJ_CPU=1`, `-np 1`). Viable but zero headroom.\n- PQ2_0 @ 262K: 7.21 + 16.0 ≈ 24.2+ GB → does NOT fit F16 KV. With `-ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0` (32 KiB/tok → 8 GiB): 15.2–16.2 GB → fits easily. With `BONSAI_KV4=1` (4-bit KV, ~16 KiB/tok → 4 GiB): ~11–12 GB.\n- 192K (196,608 tok): F16 KV = 11.7 GiB → PTQ1_0 ≈ 18.7 GB ✓, PQ2_0 ≈ 20 GB ✓ both fit fully offloaded.\n- Concurrency: KV scales per slot. At 32K/q8 KV (2 GiB/slot): PTQ1_0 fits ~6–7 slots; at 131K/q8 (4 GiB/slot): 2–3 slots; 262K = 1 slot.\n- BONSAI_KV4 uses a 4-bit KV with optional calibration bias (`scripts/make_kv_bias.sh`).\n\n5. SERVER API\n- Native OpenAI-compatible via llama-server: `/v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/completions`, `GET /v1/models`; response `timings` carries `predicted_per_second`, `draft_n`, `draft_n_accepted`. Model id: any string (single loaded model).\n\n6. PUBLISHED BENCH PROTOCOL (in-repo)\n- `community-benchmarks/ternary-bonsai/TERNARY-TEMPLATE-llama-cpp.md`: llama-bench, `-ngl 99 -fa 1`, report PP512 + TG128 raw tables, both packings. Measured RTX 3090 numbers already exist (`cuda-rtx3090-linux.md`, CachyOS, Ryzen 3800X, build 9a9394a89 = b10709): 27B PQ2_0 PP512 1477.96 / TG128 80.49 t/s; 27B Q2_g64 PP 1505.82 / TG 77.75; 8B PQ2_0 PP 5380 / TG 230.3.\n\n7. RISK FLAGS\n- CUDA 13.3 build crashes on some Linux systems (segfault) — use CUDA 12.8 build (#222, open).\n- AVX-512 CPU host segfault on load of PQ2_0 — fixed in source (#245 merged 2026-09-23); build from source at current `prism` branch to be safe.\n- sm_86: fully supported — community 3090 bench (CUDA 13.3 UMD, driver 610.57.04) ran full offload fine; prebuilt CUDA binaries cover sm_86; no patched CUDA needed. (RTX 5090/sm_120 has erratic prebuilts — not our card.)\n- \"Connection resets or crashes with quantized KV cache at very long contexts (~200K tokens)\" — reported, under investigation (KNOWN_ISSUES.md, unreproduced). Directly relevant to 192K/262K runs.\n- q5_0 KV cache several× slower — avoid; use f16/q8_0/q4_0.\n- Empty/cut-off answers common: needs `-n 16384`+ and generous `-c` (reasoning counts against output limit); thinking dominates latency — cap with `--reasoning-budget`.\n- Malformed tool calls / template quirks (exactly one system message first; empty args must be `\"{}\"`); context grows + prompt-cache misses in tool loops (Bonsai-demo#183).\n- No official drafter for Bonsai 2 27B (spec-decode unsupported officially).\n\n════════════════════════════════════════════\nB) Upstream llama.cpp — Qwen3.8-27B Unsloth UD-Q4_K_XL @ 262K on 24GB\n════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n1. REPO + VERSION\n- Repo: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp. Latest release v0.6.0 (commit d81235049384534c167caea52b85a694f6103d14, 2026-10-05); nightly build b11429. GGUF support for qwen3_5/qwen3_8 arch is stock; no fork needed (UD quants are standard IQ/K quants).\n\n2. BUILD / SERVE (exact)\n  git clone https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp && cd llama.cpp\n  cmake -B build -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF -DGGML_CUDA=ON -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=86\n  cmake --build build --config Release -j --target llama-cli llama-server llama-bench\nServe:\n  ./build/bin/llama-server \\\n    -m Qwen3.8-27B-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf \\\n    -ngl 99 -fa on -c 131072 -np 1 \\\n    -ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0 \\\n    --jinja --port 8080 \\\n    --temp 1.0 --top-p 0.95 --top-k 20 --min-p 0.0          # thinking mode\n    # instruct: --temp 0.7 --top-p 0.80 --top-k 20 --min-p 0.0 --presence-penalty 1.5\n    # reasoning effort: --chat-template-kwargs '{\"reasoning_effort\":\"medium\"}' (xhigh default)\n- Context: `-c` up to 262144 native (1M with YaRN: `--rope-scaling yarn` etc.). Concurrency: `-np N` (KV per slot; `--cont-batching` default on). \n- Spec-decode (MTP, official): `-md MTP/mtp-Qwen3.8-27B-Q4_0.gguf --spec-type draft-mtp --spec-draft-n-max 2` (Unsloth: sweep n_max 1–6, 2 is best starting point; ~1.4–2.2× decode; costs ~1.3 GB draft weights + ~2 GB F16 draft-KV headroom; measured +47% prose / +93% code on 4070 Ti, output divergence at temp>0). Also `--spec-type ngram-simple/-mod` draftless options. Qwen3.8-27B MTP GGUF confirmed present in the unsloth repo (see artifact list).\n- Quant/artifact selection: `-hf unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_XL` or hf download with `--include \"*UD-Q4_K_XL*\"`.\n\n3. ARTIFACT (HF `unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF`, apache-2.0, Dynamic 3.0, imatrix; 6.5M downloads)\n- `Qwen3.8-27B-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf` — 17,559,178,144 bytes = 16.36 GiB (17.56 GB)\n- Sibling candidates if 262K needed: `UD-IQ4_XS` 14,252,845,984 B (13.27 GiB), `UD-Q3_K_XL` 13,146,393,504 B (12.24 GiB), `UD-Q4_K_S` 15,358,213,024 B, `UD-Q4_K_M` 16,464,440,224 B.\n- MTP drafter: `MTP/mtp-Qwen3.8-27B-Q4_0.gguf` — 1,369,590,656 B (1.28 GiB).\n- Vision (optional): `mmproj-F16.gguf` 927,607,488 B / `mmproj-BF16.gguf` 931,146,432 B.\n- Download: `hf download unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF --include \"*UD-Q4_K_XL*\" --include \"MTP/*\" --local-dir .`\n- Arch (from model card): 27B, 64 layers, hidden layout 16×(3×(Gated DeltaNet→FFN)→1×(Gated Attention→FFN)); Gated Attention 4 KV heads × 256 head_dim → only 16 layers carry KV → 64 KiB/token F16 (same math as Bonsai 2). Context 262,144 natively, YaRN-extensible to 1M.\n\n4. 24GB VRAM FIT @ 262K (the decisive check)\n- UD-Q4_K_XL 16.36 GiB weights + 262K KV: F16 16 GiB → ~33.6 GB NO; q8_0 KV 8 GiB → ~26.4 GB NO; q4_0 KV 4 GiB → ~22.4 GB + compute buffers → borderline-NO on 24576 MiB. **UD-Q4_K_XL at 262K does NOT fit 24GB without CPU offload**; it is NOT a viable 262K artifact.\n- Practical maxima for UD-Q4_K_XL on 24GB: `-c 131072 -ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0` ≈ 22.4 GB ✓ (1 slot); `-c 196608` needs q4_0 KV ≈ 21.8 GB ✓ barely; `-c 262144` only with q4_0 KV and prayer. With MTP enabled subtract ~2 GB more headroom.\n- If 262K@24GB is a hard requirement for Qwen3.8: use `UD-IQ4_XS` (13.27 GiB + q8_0 KV 8 GiB ≈ 22.3 GB ✓, or q4_0 KV 19.3 GB comfortable) or `UD-Q3_K_XL` (12.24 GiB → roomy). Unsloth itself steers 262K-class long-context on 24 GB to smaller quants; 4-bit class is \"16–19 GB total\" per their table without long-context KV.\n- Concurrency on 24GB: UD-Q4_K_XL @ 32K/q8 KV (2 GiB/slot): ~2–3 slots; @ 8K: 4–6 slots.\n\n5. SERVER API\n- Standard llama-server OpenAI-compatible `/v1/chat/completions` (+ `/v1/completions`, `/v1/embeddings`, `/v1/models`, web UI); `--jinja` for tool calls. v0.6.0 adds MTP batch API (`draft-mtp` verified with Qwen4Exp, and Qwen3.8 MTP is the same embedded-NextN path per Unsloth/4070Ti study on b10448).\n\n6. PUBLISHED BENCH PROTOCOL (in-repo/community)\n- Upstream repo ships `llama-bench` (pp512/tg128, `--spec-synth-*` synthetic-acceptance options for spec benches) and `tools/server` `timings` (prompt_per_second / predicted_per_second / TTFT) — no HF-side official scripts.\n- Best external protocol: hugosmoreira/qwen38-27b-rtx4070ti-windows-benchmark (pinned llama.cpp b10448; q8 KV; measures prompt tok/s, gen tok/s, TTFT, peak VRAM at 250 ms telemetry). Data points on 12GB: UD-Q2_K_XL 66/66 layers, 4K ctx: 38.0 t/s gen, 10.56 GB peak; MTP +47–93%. IQ4_XS near-64K on 12GB: ~301 s TTFT, 1.57 t/s decode — long-context on small VRAM collapses decode; expect far better on 24GB but 262K still untested publicly.\n\n7. RISK FLAGS\n- No 24GB/262K success report found for UD-Q4_K_XL specifically; community evidence covers 12GB cards at ≤16K (UD-IQ2/Q2) — the 262K-attempt on 24GB is effectively unexplored territory with expected failure at q8 KV and knife-edge at q4_0 KV.\n- Qwen3.8 KV quant + flash attention: use `-fa on` with `-ctk/-ctv`; avoid q5_0 KV (generic llama.cpp+PrismML perf note).\n- Thinking mode burns tokens fast (xhigh default): bound with `--reasoning-budget`/`reasoning_effort` or empty-answer reports recur (`-n 16384`+ recommended).\n- sm_86: fully supported upstream (CUDA CI covers Ampere); MTP path tested on CUDA (4070 Ti study used official CUDA 13.3 build b10448). No patched CUDA required. `--split-mode tensor/row` multi-GPU quirks exist but irrelevant single-GPU.\n- Unsloth warns: dynamic quants refreshed to Dynamic 3.0 on Aug 19, 2026 — pin the HF revision (current file tree oid c8952f5e7d1c817e59f2d2f9c10121b5e81cc1e3) for reproducibility.\n\nVERDICT SNAPSHOT FOR THE CAMPAIGN\n- Bonsai 2 27B PTQ1_0: 262K/24GB fits (barely, F16 KV, np1) — unique among candidates; 192K comfortable; no official spec-decode.\n- Bonsai 2 27B PQ2_0: 262K needs q8 KV (fits well); fastest PP.\n- Qwen3.8 UD-Q4_K_XL: NOT viable at 262K/24GB; viable ≤131K (q8 KV). UD-IQ4_XS is the 262K-capable Qwen3.8 fallback. MTP spec-decode available and cheap (+1.28 GB drafter).\n- PrismML fork binaries: use CUDA 12.8 Linux build of prism-b10754-2459f68 (13.3 crashes reported); upstream: v0.6.0/b11429."
